    "sections": [
      {
        "label": "1st period",
        "score": "ANA 2, BOS 0",
        "text": "Anaheim controlled the period and struck twice in the final 38 seconds. Tim Washe's wrist shot from above the left circle went through a screen at 19:22, and 21 seconds later Beckett Sennecke redirected a Nikita Nesterenko feed for a 2–0 lead."
      },
      {
        "label": "2nd period",
        "score": "ANA 2, BOS 1",
        "text": "Frederic Brunet cut it to 2–1 at 3:15 with a power-play snap shot from just inside the blue line, his first NHL goal. Late in the period Nikita Zadorov was penalized for elbowing and roughing Frank Vatrano, and Boston opened the third still short-handed."
      },
      {
        "label": "3rd period",
        "score": "Final: BOS 4, ANA 2",
        "text": "David Pastrnak tied it 2–2 at 3:26, backhanding a loose puck into an open net after Noah Warren broke up an Elias Lindholm pass. Lindholm scored from in front of the crease on the power play at 8:18 for Boston's first lead, 3–2, and Matthew Poitras finished a 2-on-1 with James Hagens at 16:20 for the 4–2 final. Boston went 3-for-4 on the power play; Anaheim went 0-for-5."
      }
    ],
